{
  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt+resnet50, weighted fusion → 42.1% accuracy), the critical uncertainty is how much each modality contributes individually. Config_028 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image branch using the exact same image encoder and profile setting as config_009, enabling a direct comparison. If image-only accuracy is near 42%, RNA adds little and the fusion strategy is the bottleneck; if it is substantially lower, RNA is a meaningful contributor and we should focus on improving RNA encoding or fusion. Resolving this modality-contribution question early is essential for allocating the remaining 8 experiments efficiently toward the right design dimensions (fusion, multiprofile, encoder upgrades) rather than chasing a modality that may be underperforming."
}

